'' A statement-lifetime temporary dies where fbc flushes its destructor list: after each
'' PRINT / WRITE / PRINT USING item, channel and format, each DIM declarator, each FOR head
'' expression, and an IF, ELSEIF, SELECT subject or CASE value before its branch. A byval
'' copy or a conversion temporary joins that list. Runtime output was checked against
'' fbc-modern; see the source's header.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/udt-stmt-temp-life.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: verify: ok
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered
'' GOLDEN: expected/udt-stmt-temp-life.out
